course: dictionary
lesson: 8585
title: Meet the scientist
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A scientist is a person who studies the natural world. They ask questions, make careful observations and do experiments. Then they use evidence, which means facts you can check, to find out how things work.
explain: In science lessons you can «work like a scientist». First you ask a question, then you predict an answer, plan a fair test, measure, record your results and draw a conclusion. A conclusion is what your results show.
explain: Scientists also change their minds. When new evidence shows an idea was wrong, a good scientist changes the idea. Scientists only «say» something new when the evidence supports it.
fact: A scientist is a person who studies the natural world by asking questions, making careful observations and doing experiments.
fact: Famous scientists include Marie Curie, Isaac Newton and Charles Darwin.
fact: Kinds of scientists include biologists, chemists, physicists and astronomers.
fact: «In Siberia scientists bred only the tamest foxes for over 60 years»: the foxes became friendly, and some even got floppy ears.
fact: Rangers and scientists study droppings to learn which animals live in a place and what they eat.
exercise: What is the name for a person who studies the natural world by asking questions and doing experiments? | A tailor | A referee | A poet | *A scientist
exercise: «Rangers and scientists study droppings to learn which animals live in a place.» What do scientists use droppings to find out? | Which colour paint looks best | Whether it will rain tomorrow | How to cook a meal | *Which animals live in a place and what they eat
exercise: When you work like a scientist, what do you do right after you predict an answer? | Forget the question | Eat your lunch | *Plan a fair test | Decide the answer must always be true
test: Why do scientists change their ideas? | Because the idea was too short | Because they get bored of them | Because they want to be famous | *Because new evidence shows the idea was wrong
test: «Since then scientists make sure the person testing an animal does not know the answer.» Why is this done? | To save money on food | *So nobody can give hints by accident | So the animal knows what to do | To make the test longer
exam: «A good scientist checks a story before repeating it.» What does this tell you a scientist does? | Makes up stories for fun | Believes every story they hear | *Checks evidence before they trust or repeat something | Repeats stories as fast as they can
